      "created_at": "2013-06-07T02:51:49.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Koey\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/koey/48/2187_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Koey:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Guessing it was asked is because Divine Sacrifice is a One Shot.\"Fanatic Deals Up to 3 Targets 1 Irreducible Radiant Damage Each.\"\"Damage dealt by Those Targets is Redirected to Fanatic until the Start of your Next Turn.\"&nbsp;&nbsp;I think that card is preceise enough it might actually redirect to Fanatic even if she is Incapped. Cause incapped Heroes still have their Start of Turn.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Yeah, this is kind of what I was thinking when I questioned it at all: the fact that it was a one-shot and not an ongoing, and the fact that she still had a start of turn. But then \"no longer a valid target\" and \"no longer named Fanatic\" arguments both convince me.</p>",
